       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the problem. 6000 mg/day is well above the maximum safe daily dose, and a 2000 mg single dose is double the usual maximum. Entering it could cause real harm to your patient.\n\nYou have a few ways forward:\n- **Enter a safe regimen now.** I can enter 1000 mg PO three times daily (3000 mg/day) or four times daily (4000 mg/day). I can also add a note about the pain target or duration.\n- **Check with your resident or attending.** If you think a higher dose is needed, they can review it. If they decide it's justified, they can enter or co-sign it themselves through the proper channels. The pharmacy can also help with the dosing question.\n- **Add other pain control.** If 4000 mg/day of acetaminophen isn't enough, your team can add another analgesic. I can enter that once they've chosen one.\n\nTell me which regimen you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
